<title>GREECE: UPDATE: EXPIRIES OF GREEK GOVT DEBT SECURITIES IN JULY.</title>
<headline>UPDATE: EXPIRIES OF GREEK GOVT DEBT SECURITIES IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is information on the</p>
<p>expiries of Greece's drachma and foreign currency denominated</p>
<p>government debt in July.</p>
<p>	ISSUE DATE	  AMOUNT RAISED	  COUPON</p>
<p>  July  1, 1996  173 billion drachmas	 13.30%</p>
<p>  July 15, 1994	  7,698,000 marks	 6.95%</p>
<p>  July 17, 1996  155 billion drachmas  13% (12-mth T-bill)</p>
<p>  July 31, 1992   97 billion drachmas    12-mth T-bill</p>
<p>  July 31, 1996  258 billion drachmas  12.80% (12-mth T-bill)</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
